{#
settings/_reading_pane.html.twig
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Where the open message goes: in place of the list (Off, which is how plMail
always worked) or beside it.

A page of its own under Features, not a control on Appearance where it first
lived. Appearance is the look of the app — one JSON payload that becomes an
exported theme — and this is something the mailbox DOES. It sat there as the
one control on the page that was not part of the theme, with a paragraph
explaining why not.

Posted by `settings--reading-pane` to its own endpoint, with its own token
(see AppearanceController::readingPaneState), and not a form that submits and
redirects like the shortcuts card beside it: that endpoint is also what the
divider on the mailbox posts its width to, so it answers JSON for both.

The divider that sets how much each pane gets is on the mailbox itself, where
it can be dragged against real mail. There is no slider for it here.

Accepts:
  mode  App\Domain\Enum\Mail\ReadingPaneMode  the user's current choice
#}
{% set segText = 'flex h-full items-center justify-center px-3 py-1.5 text-center text-[11px] leading-tight text-ink-muted
                  peer-checked:bg-accent peer-checked:text-accent-ink
                  peer-focus-visible:ring-2 peer-focus-visible:ring-inset peer-focus-visible:ring-accent
                  transition-colors cursor-pointer' %}

<div class="px-4 py-3"
     data-controller="settings--reading-pane"
     data-settings--reading-pane-url-value="{{ path('app_appearance_reading_pane_state') }}"
     data-settings--reading-pane-token-value="{{ csrf_token('reading_pane_state') }}">
    <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3">
        <span class="min-w-0">
            <span class="block text-xs font-medium text-ink-muted" id="reading-pane-label">{{ 'settings.reading_pane.label'|trans }}</span>
            <span class="block text-[11px] text-ink-faint mt-0.5">{{ 'settings.reading_pane.hint'|trans }}</span>
        </span>

        <div class="grid grid-flow-col auto-cols-fr shrink-0 rounded-pane border border-line overflow-hidden"
             role="radiogroup" aria-labelledby="reading-pane-label">
            {% for case in enum('App\\Domain\\Enum\\Mail\\ReadingPaneMode').cases %}
                <label>
                    <input type="radio" name="readingPane" class="peer sr-only"
                           value="{{ case.value }}"
                           data-action="change->settings--reading-pane#pick"
                           aria-label="{{ ('settings.reading_pane.' ~ case.value)|trans }}"
                           {{ mode == case ? 'checked' : '' }}>
                    <span class="{{ segText }}">
                        {{ ('settings.reading_pane.' ~ case.value)|trans }}
                    </span>
                </label>
            {% endfor %}
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
